```
If `url` has a trailing path (e.g., `https://chat.example.com/some/path`), the `new URL` constructor would resolve the relative path against it, potentially producing a wrong URL. The code does `url.replace(/\/+$/, "")` before persisting, but the probe uses the raw `url` before that replacement.

Wait, looking at the code flow:
```javascript
